219
00:11:32,157 --> 00:11:33,877
It's called a log pose.

220
00:11:34,517 --> 00:11:34,837
Huh?

221
00:11:35,017 --> 00:11:36,957
Your standard compass doesn't work here,

222
00:11:37,057 --> 00:11:39,237
so we have to use the island's magnetic fields.

223
00:11:39,557 --> 00:11:41,677
And that is the tool we use to follow them.

224
00:11:42,217 --> 00:11:45,537
It's the only way that it's even possible to navigate the Grand Line.

225
00:11:47,957 --> 00:11:50,057
Excuse me, Miss, do you have any suggestions

226
00:11:50,057 --> 00:11:52,697
on how I can get back to my restaurant in the East Blue?

227
00:11:52,697 --> 00:11:54,997
The last thing I need is to lose my job.

228
00:11:55,157 --> 00:11:56,317
You don't want to do that.

229
00:11:56,317 --> 00:11:59,137
Trust me, it's taken us a ridiculously long time

230
00:11:59,137 --> 00:12:00,537
to reach this point in our journey.

231
00:12:00,857 --> 00:12:02,457
Heading back on your own would be suicide.

232
00:12:03,857 --> 00:12:04,957
Just take a look.

233
00:12:05,457 --> 00:12:08,657
We've been following the log pose coordinates for quite some time,

234
00:12:08,937 --> 00:12:11,977
and they've led us directly to this coral reef-surrounded island.

235
00:12:12,797 --> 00:12:15,777
You don't actually expect me to believe any of this, do you?

236
00:12:16,297 --> 00:12:18,637
Why would I possibly travel with a group of people

237
00:12:18,637 --> 00:12:20,137
I have nothing in common with?

238
00:12:20,597 --> 00:12:21,397
That's why.

239
00:12:26,317 --> 00:12:29,037
Hey, wait, isn't that a pirate flag?

240
00:12:29,357 --> 00:12:31,357
You mean we're on a pirate ship?

241
00:12:31,857 --> 00:12:33,277
I already told you,

242
00:12:33,337 --> 00:12:35,877
you're on the intrepid Captain Usopp's pirate ship.

243
00:12:36,077 --> 00:12:37,077
For real?

244
00:12:38,737 --> 00:12:40,877
You know what's kind of odd, Captain Usopp?

245
00:12:41,257 --> 00:12:44,277
The fact that your Jolly Roger is wearing a straw hat.

246
00:12:44,437 --> 00:12:44,697
Huh?

247
00:12:45,237 --> 00:12:45,837
It is?

248
00:12:46,377 --> 00:12:49,117
Uh, that's because this hat is mine.

249
00:12:49,277 --> 00:12:50,417
Hey, no it's not!

250
00:12:50,497 --> 00:12:51,077
Give it back!

251
00:12:51,077 --> 00:12:56,937
You can touch my hat one more time

252
00:12:56,937 --> 00:12:59,057
and I'll kick your butt to the other side of the ocean!

253
00:12:59,377 --> 00:13:00,217
What's the deal?

254
00:13:00,357 --> 00:13:02,117
How can you remember that it's your hat?

255
00:13:02,277 --> 00:13:03,497
I remember all right.

256
00:13:03,617 --> 00:13:05,557
This hat is like treasure to me.

257
00:13:06,257 --> 00:13:06,617
Treasure?

258
00:13:08,837 --> 00:13:10,977
A friend gave it to me when I was little,

259
00:13:11,177 --> 00:13:12,797
and it means a whole lot.

260
00:13:13,297 --> 00:13:16,177
I swore on this hat that one day I'd become a pirate

261
00:13:16,177 --> 00:13:18,037
and gather up my own crew.

262
00:13:18,037 --> 00:13:21,617
Pirate this, pirate that, who cares?

263
00:13:22,497 --> 00:13:24,617
Although, one thing is certain now.

264
00:13:25,117 --> 00:13:28,117
Everything you've told us is a big steaming pile of nonsense.

265
00:13:29,337 --> 00:13:30,697
I hate pirates!

266
00:13:30,777 --> 00:13:32,297
Every stinking last one of them!

267
00:13:32,777 --> 00:13:34,417
So why would I be on this ship?

268
00:13:34,677 --> 00:13:37,117
The only things I love are money and tangerines,

269
00:13:37,197 --> 00:13:38,677
and I don't see either around here.

270
00:13:39,197 --> 00:13:41,577
Hey now, I don't really see any reason

271
00:13:41,577 --> 00:13:43,317
for you to be so rude to us.

272
00:13:43,317 --> 00:13:47,857
Tangerines?

273
00:13:48,157 --> 00:13:49,277
Like those?

274
00:13:55,777 --> 00:13:57,537
Why are those on a ship?

275
00:13:57,537 --> 00:14:05,097
What just happened?

276
00:14:05,437 --> 00:14:05,717
Ah!

277
00:14:05,937 --> 00:14:07,257
That tree grew an arm!

278
00:14:07,577 --> 00:14:08,997
A mystery tree!

279
00:14:09,397 --> 00:14:10,797
Just who the hell are you?

280
00:14:11,217 --> 00:14:13,477
Aren't you a bit more curious about that?

281
00:14:13,717 --> 00:14:15,957
I can tell it's one of Bellomere's tangerines.

282
00:14:16,057 --> 00:14:16,917
I'd know them anywhere.

283
00:14:17,117 --> 00:14:19,677
But what exactly are they doing here aboard this ship?

